{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic","id":713756,"title":"Blood & Smoke and Blood Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T23:01:45-07:00","id":713756,"title":"Blood & Smoke and Blood Magic","content":"\u200bSo i'm starting my first game of vampire (previously they have guest starred in my mage games), and my first game of the nWoD 2e rules.<br /> <br /> I mostly like all the new rules. A lot of good improvements, but one of my concerns or just queries is how the new rules interact with the Blood Magic book. I liked Blood Magic personally, I felt it really opened up vampire, and it allowed them to compete better/survive with the other supernatural entities. Now I realise in the new rules that's not such an issue. Vampires are just so much more deadly, I also believe they changed/improved the blood magics. Its one of the areas I've not yet thad a chance tot have a look at.<br /> <br /> So does Blood &amp; Smoke completely write off the Blood Magic book, does it still go together well or does it need a bitt of work?<br /> <br /> appreciate your answers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1510-mysticjackal","name":"MysticJackal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:03:25-07:00","id":713773,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about this too. I've seen Blood Magic recommended as a good supplement for Requiem 2e, so I assume it fits well, but would love to see a more detailed discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:26:52-07:00","id":713800,"title":"","content":"The 2e system for blood magic is based on the rules from <i>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</i>. They don't reproduce the rules for Themes and Ritual Factors in the Blood &amp; Smoke/2e book, but they used that system to determine the target numbers of successes. The biggest difference is that rituals take longer in 2e. Each roll in the extended action represents 30 minutes, rather than 1 turn (though it's reduced to 15 minutes of you have more dots in the Discipline than the dot rating of the ritual.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:55:59-07:00","id":714161,"title":"","content":"Personally I always found <i>BS:SaB</i> too overpowered. When blood sorcerers can almost stand toe to toe with Awakened in pure magick terms, plus having their own vampire powers, you have a balance problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:12:14-07:00","id":714208,"title":"","content":"I knew there was something I liked about Requiem over Masquerade. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually lots of things, but there's a certain <i>frisson</i> if blood sorcerers can outdo mages.<br /> <br /> Even so, I'd wait for Mage 2e for any final determination on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:23:30-07:00","id":714220,"title":"","content":"I felt the bigger problem there was the base roll interval of <i>turns</i>, honestly. Which was something carried over from the 1e core rather than the fault of BS, and did blood sorcery no favors with how it didn't feel ritual.<br /> <br /> The book really did have some silly things going on with ritual factors though. (Was discussing this recently with someone: RAW a Cruac practitioner who had mastered Creation would not have had difficulty in birthing a ghouled t-rex because the base Size factor of spells was 20.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:31:52-07:00","id":714226,"title":"","content":"I can't shake the feeling that at least some of the 2e rituals were written<i> before </i>they decided to make the rolls 30 minutes long. Because while they'd work if the casting time was a few seconds, they're just awkward to use, or in some cases pointless.<br /> <br /> Take Stigmata for instance. That does a few points of lethal damage to someone who has to be there while you cast it. Which at 5 successes could take over an <i>hour. </i>Besides the spectacle, there's absolutely no reason to use it instead of just, y'know, stabbing them. And I don't really think a party trick is worth four dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-22-2015, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:48:48-07:00","id":714250,"title":"","content":"I like how they did it for 2e, but for those reasons and others I think it could benefit from having ways to increment rituals traits (like delaying an effect and adding a trigger for it \u00e0 la Divination 2 in BS).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:04:48-07:00","id":714285,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that seems like the best way to do it. It's a bit Vancian, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:22:16-07:00","id":714304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714220#post714220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book really did have some silly things going on with ritual factors though. (Was discussing this recently with someone: RAW a Cruac practitioner who had mastered Creation would not have had difficulty in birthing a ghouled t-rex because the base Size factor of spells was 20.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the rules were based on Mage: the Awakening first edition, where the base Size factor was also 20. When Mage second edition arrives, I'd recommend changing the basic spell factors and other things based on Mage to the new baseline unless you want Vampires to be better mages than actual mages in some cases.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, the new basic Size factor for Mage will be 5, which sounds much more reasonable than 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:25:09-07:00","id":714310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714226#post714226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't shake the feeling that at least some of the 2e rituals were written<i> before </i>they decided to make the rolls 30 minutes long. Because while they'd work if the casting time was a few seconds, they're just awkward to use, or in some cases pointless.<br /> <br /> Take Stigmata for instance. That does a few points of lethal damage to someone who has to be there while you cast it. Which at 5 successes could take over an <i>hour. </i>Besides the spectacle, there's absolutely no reason to use it instead of just, y'know, stabbing them. And I don't really think a party trick is worth four dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpreted once the ritual was finished, it remained charged hold until the sorcerer decided to unleash its effects (in the same night, for a number of hours equal the Cruac dots, or something similar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-22-2015, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:31:09-07:00","id":714343,"title":"","content":"Just have it til sunrise. Vamps running round loaded with spells like an oldschool DnD wizard, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T07:48:28-07:00","id":714512,"title":"","content":"Also, I remember in the <i>Circle of the Crone</i> supplement how different factions could have different versions of the same rituals. Ex: a japanese mahou tsukai didn\u00b4t need to see the victim to perform Cheval, but having a point of her vitae obtained the same night.<br /> So, you may rule out all rituals can be also performed throught Symphathy, specially throught blood, but maybe also nails or hair. Imagine a paranoid kindred refusing going to a reunion with the local acolytes without a vacuum cleaner. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-22-2015, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:55:20-07:00","id":714650,"title":"","content":"I think Elfive's right, that some stuff was changed near the end and other stuff wasn't changed to match it.<br /> <br /> There were several threads when Blood &amp; Smoke just came out about blood sorcery, a number with 'patches,' and I believe we ended up using one that sort of switched the times around between rites and improvised magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:56:36-07:00","id":714712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714226#post714226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't shake the feeling that at least some of the 2e rituals were written<i> before </i>they decided to make the rolls 30 minutes long. Because while they'd work if the casting time was a few seconds, they're just awkward to use, or in some cases pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>They all were. They're the exact same rituals from the 1e core book. They decided to use the Sacrements and Blasphemies rules for determining target number of successes for rituals, but with the casting times fixed, because the improvised casting rules were broken with a duration of turns. Of course, since the rituals they put in the 2e core were written to work with the 1e blood sorcery system, they don't really work quite right when they're ported over to the 2e system.<br /> <br /> The rites and miracles previewed from Secrets of the Covenants are much more in line with 2e's blood sorcery system, and Sacrements and Blasphemies' improvised casting rules make great guidelines for creating custom 2e rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714650#post714650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were several threads when Blood &amp; Smoke just came out about blood sorcery, a number with 'patches,' and I believe we ended up using one that sort of switched the times around between rites and improvised magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting times are the same with improvised and learned rituals, but most people switch the dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:46:26-07:00","id":714772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714343#post714343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just have it til sunrise. Vamps running round loaded with spells like an oldschool DnD wizard, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could lead to a new neopagan fashion resurgence. Members of the circle going around with not just the usual underplayed rings or pendants, but exaggerated, colorful occult symbolism, as an unsubtle reminder to their rivals and foes that, potentially, at any moment, <i>Magic Missiles</i> could be a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 10-22-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:53:45-07:00","id":714786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714712#post714712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting times are the same with improvised and learned rituals, but most people switch the dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was it, yeah, it's been a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714772#post714772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could lead to a new neopagan fashion resurgence. Members of the circle going around with not just the usual underplayed rings or pendants, but exaggerated, colorful occult symbolism, as an unsubtle reminder to their rivals and foes that, potentially, at any moment, <i>Magic Missiles</i> could be a possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Theban rite, Vitae Reliquary, that allows you to store your Vitae in an object, letting you turn that object into Vitae so you can ingest it later if you need. There's a scene in the Strix Chronicles Anthology where Maxwell and Solomon are going after Old John, expecting a fight, and Maxwell has at least eight of these Vitae reliquaries on him.<br /> <br /> It makes perfect sense. But it struck me as a little weird.<br /> <br /> Still, people come at the game wanting and expecting different things. If you don't want a 'magicky' character, you just choose a character who doesn't do blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:57:30-07:00","id":714982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714786#post714786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a scene in the Strix Chronicles Anthology where Maxwell and Solomon are going after Old John, expecting a fight, and Maxwell has at least eight of these Vitae reliquaries on him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell me the name of this tale? I think I lost it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:49:56-07:00","id":715138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714982#post714982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you tell me the name of this tale? I think I lost it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it was added in later, because when I first read the anthology I completely missed it, and I usually read through everything. I didn't notice it until someone mentioned a story about Prince Maxwell in it a couple months ago on the forum and went back and check. <i>But</i>, I don't like Solomon Birch and it starts off focusing on him so I might have just skipped it and forgotten to go back.<br /> <br /> It's called <i>Four Years, Old John</i>, by Greg Stolze. It's on page 47 of the pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:36:03-07:00","id":718815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MysticJackal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic#post713756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo does Blood &amp; Smoke completely write off the Blood Magic book, does it still go together well or does it need a bitt of work?<br /> <br /> appreciate your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>While its theoretically possible to use the Blasphemies and Sacrament book, it seems like its not really going to be used going forwards. Yes, both the 2e rules and the Blood Magic book took their cues from Mage, so the new core book is theoretically compatable. However, the rituals from the core book don't <i>quite</i> work well with the new rules, and the rituals we've seen teased from the Secrets of the Covenant writers don't quite fit perfectly with the new stuff, and it definitely seems like they're not using the Blood Magic book for guidelines.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think that you're going to need to do some work no matter what you do with the blood magic to fit what you want with your chronicle. Personally, I prefer just using the Sacraments and Blasphemies book for ritual ideas, and then converting them over. Fits with how the rest of the covenants buy up their abilities. Allowing Themes could easily make Law, Oaths, and Coils redundant, which is problematic for players who like those covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-23-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:01:26-07:00","id":719205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=714786#post714786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was it, yeah, it's been a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a Theban rite, Vitae Reliquary, that allows you to store your Vitae in an object, letting you turn that object into Vitae so you can ingest it later if you need. There's a scene in the Strix Chronicles Anthology where Maxwell and Solomon are going after Old John, expecting a fight, and Maxwell has at least eight of these Vitae reliquaries on him.<br /> <br /> It makes perfect sense. But it struck me as a little weird.<br /> <br /> Still, people come at the game wanting and expecting different things. If you don't want a 'magicky' character, you just choose a character who doesn't do blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Masquerade, My character used just such a tactic, using a Rosary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:45:45-07:00","id":725025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=718815#post718815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While its theoretically possible to use the Blasphemies and Sacrament book, it seems like its not really going to be used going forwards. Yes, both the 2e rules and the Blood Magic book took their cues from Mage, so the new core book is theoretically compatable. However, the rituals from the core book don't <i>quite</i> work well with the new rules, and the rituals we've seen teased from the Secrets of the Covenant writers don't quite fit perfectly with the new stuff, and it definitely seems like they're not using the Blood Magic book for guidelines.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think that you're going to need to do some work no matter what you do with the blood magic to fit what you want with your chronicle. Personally, I prefer just using the Sacraments and Blasphemies book for ritual ideas, and then converting them over. Fits with how the rest of the covenants buy up their abilities. Allowing Themes could easily make Law, Oaths, and Coils redundant, which is problematic for players who like those covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is really going to bug me. I love the Dynamic Rules . While I have no problem with them being optional. Having to rewrite every new supplement to use is going to be a pain.<br /> It might even force not to buy new blood magick related supplements if I in the must rewrite my own. Might as well just homebrew it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T21:29:43-07:00","id":725143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=725025#post725025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is really going to bug me. I love the Dynamic Rules . While I have no problem with them being optional. Having to rewrite every new supplement to use is going to be a pain.<br /> It might even force not to buy new blood magick related supplements if I in the must rewrite my own. Might as well just homebrew it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could just declare that improvised rituals follow slightly different rules (ala Blasphemies) and the designed Rites have lost lore involved or been blessed by another power, etc.<br /> Yes it makes it hard to exactly replicate effects you've seen but not learned. That provides a reason to seek out known sorcerous ritematsers rather than trying to improve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T22:08:49-07:00","id":725184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713756-blood-smoke-and-blood-magic?p=725143#post725143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could just declare that improvised rituals follow slightly different rules (ala Blasphemies) and the designed Rites have lost lore involved or been blessed by another power, etc.<br /> Yes it makes it hard to exactly replicate effects you've seen but not learned. That provides a reason to seek out known sorcerous ritematsers rather than trying to improve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of like what I do in my games, but in reverse. The 2e rules are the standard, and as far as most practitioners know, only way to do blood magic. Improvising rituals is a secret, lost art that an intrepid character might be able to beseech dark forces to learn, and uses the Sacriments and Blasphemies rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T20:28:49-07:00","id":730928,"title":"","content":"In my games I reversed the improvised/learned pools. Improvised magic relies on the listed theme dice pools so requires more branching out to be effective unless your focused on one theme. I also allow learned rituals to be cast without the prerequisite themes, so long as the appropriate Cruac/Theban level is met. (If you know a Transmutation 5 ritual, Have Theban 5, but only Transmutation 3, you can still cast it). I still have the lost successes rule also (Improvised cannot have additional incremental effects, they're measured not rote quality).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}